+"""Multi-slot prefill for GLM-5.3-Flash's batch scheduler (patches/0560, GLM53_TF_MULTI_PREFILL, default 0).
+
+Why
+---
+A short prompt's prefill is weight-read bound: a 130-row fast chunk reads nearly every routed expert (130 rows x 8
+picks over 288 experts touch ~97% of them, ~74 GB a rank of the ~76 GB, docs/ROOFLINE.md: U(R) x 0.264 GB), so
+four such prompts prefilled one after another (patches/0200's ``GLM53_TF_BATCH_SHORT``, RigMark C4) read the experts
+four times: W13 measured 0.41 s a piece and first tokens at 0.47 / 0.9 / 1.3 / 1.7 s (0540: each first token as its
+piece ends). With this knob the pieces of one round go through ONE forward: their rows stacked (each prompt's rows
+contiguous), every per-sequence part per slot, the routed experts once over all the rows.
+
+What a group forward is (``compute``)
+-------------------------------------
+The lean fast chunk (patches/0082) whose sub-blocks are the members' own: member i's rows sit at [off_i, off_i + R_i)
+of the lean set and are cut into sub-blocks of ``GLM53_TF_LEAN_BLOCK`` rows FROM ITS OWN START (``blocks``), so a
+sub-block never holds rows of two prompts and a member's sub-blocks are exactly the ones its lone chunk of R_i rows
+would run. Per sub-block (member i, local row la, absolute position pos_i + la) the attention half runs as in the lone
+chunk: hc_pre, the KDA block from the member's committed state (la = 0) or the carry of its previous sub-block (the
+member's own conv tail, ``tails``), the DSA block on the member's latent / index caches (patches/0290: its page
+tables) at its positions; the FFN half's hc_pre, shared expert, combine and hc_post per sub-block; the router, top-k,
+grouping and the routed experts ONCE over all T = sum R_i rows. The three production loops are covered: 0082's
+(``_plain``), 0084's pipeline (``_MultiChunk``: the same piece order, pre(k) then post(k - 1)) and 0320's row split
+(``_MultiSplit``, when the lone rule would split a chunk of T rows: T > the sub-block); the head runs on each member's
+last row (one row: qmm, as alone), into its own logits row.
+
+Exactness (each member's bits are its lone prefill's)
+------------------------------------------------------
+- every call that reads per-sequence state or positions (KDA chain, DSA write / attention / indexer, carries, commit,
+  snapshots, MTP absorb, DFlash2 taps, the head, the sample) is the member's lone call: same rows, same shapes, same
+  state, same positions (its sub-blocks are its lone sub-blocks);
+- every other call runs on a row subset that is not the lone one: hyper-connections, norms, embed, stream means
+  (per-row glue), the matmuls (``fast_qmm.matmul_fast``: tiles fixed by the weight's shape, one accumulator over K,
+  every row count on the fast kernels except the head's single row, patches/0085), the router and top-k (per row), the
+  grouping (only decides which warp holds a pair), the routed experts (``exl3_fast.cu``: a pair's mma chain is one
+  warp's ascending walk over K) and the bf16 exchanges (copies). These are exactly the kernels patches/0085's claim
+  already rests on: a fast prefill's state does not depend on its chunking because no fast kernel's result for a row
+  depends on the other rows of the call or their count. A group is one more chunking of the same rows;
+- kernel CHOICES that depend on the call's total rows: ``fast_qmm``'s < 64-row qmm fallback is gone in fast chunks
+  (0085; the head keeps it and is per member); the routed experts' mode picks by rows under
+  GLM53_TF_FAST_EXPERTS=auto (fast2 vs fat, 0270) and =once (GLM53_TF_ONCE_MIN_ROWS, 0260), each documented as the
+  same bits, but a group never relies on that: with those modes groups are not formed (``kernels_ok``). Production
+  runs ``fat`` (one kernel family for every row count). pfpp's split / pfoverlap's drain depend on the sub-block
+  count, and are the same bits (0320, 0084);
+- the order of the per-member host steps (reset / restore, marks, snapshots, absorb, taps, commit, sample, saves) is
+  the lone prefill's for each member; members never share state (their own ``State``, drafter view, snapshots). The
+  KDA projection / replay rows (``State.proj`` / ``scratch``) are slot 0's for every member (``Batcher._borrow``):
+  they hold one sub-block's rows between its projection and its chain, sub-blocks run one after another.
+
+Which pieces go together (``groups``, both ranks, from state both hold)
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------
+A round's pieces (``batchplan.pick_pieces``: short prompts fewest-left first, then the fair share's piece) are packed
+in that order into groups of the same request knobs (``knobs.HEADER`` values: the chunk kernels are knob-dependent),
+at most ``rows_max`` piece rows a group (GLM53_TF_MULTI_PREFILL_ROWS, default the lean set's rows,
+GLM53_TF_PREFILL_ROWS_MAX). A piece joins only when its request runs a fast lean prefill without image rows
+(patches/0500's virtual ids go through ``vision.active``, one table at a time), GLM53_TF_PROFILE and the 0430 dump
+are off. ``_piece`` recomputes each member's bound when its turn comes: the members after it still hold their slots,
+so only the LAST member could find itself alone (the others done at their first token) and get 0335's solo bound; it
+leaves the group when that would move its bound and no other request holds a slot. Others run alone as before. With
+GLM53_TF_MULTI_PREFILL on, a round whose fair share allows a piece may take more pieces (``more_pieces``: fewest
+tokens left first, while their rows fit ``rows_max``): prompts past ``GLM53_TF_BATCH_SHORT`` (agent bursts) share
+forwards too. GLM53_TF_MULTI_PREFILL_WAIT_MS (rank 0; default 10): when the batch is idle and fewer requests wait
+than slots are free, the plan waits up to that long after the oldest arrival for more (RigMark C4's four streams
+arrive within a few ms; without it the first is prefilled alone and the other three together).
+
+Both ranks must agree on the knob and ``rows_max`` (checked at load: they decide the forwards and collectives).
+"""
+
+from __future__ import annotations
+
+import contextlib
+import os
+import sys
+from types import SimpleNamespace
+from typing import Sequence
+
+ENV = "GLM53_TF_MULTI_PREFILL"
+ROWS_ENV = "GLM53_TF_MULTI_PREFILL_ROWS"
+WAIT_ENV = "GLM53_TF_MULTI_PREFILL_WAIT_MS"
+
+
+def parse(raw: str | None = None) -> bool:
+    raw = os.environ.get(ENV, "0") if raw is None else raw
+    v = str(raw).strip().lower()
+    if v in ("", "0", "off", "false", "no"):
+        return False
+    if v in ("1", "on", "true", "yes"):
+        return True
+    raise ValueError(f"{ENV}={raw!r}: expected 0 or 1")
+
+
+def rows_env() -> int:
+    """GLM53_TF_MULTI_PREFILL_ROWS: piece rows a group may hold (0 / unset: the lean set's rows)."""
+
+    raw = os.environ.get(ROWS_ENV, "").strip()
+    v = int(raw) if raw else 0
+    if v < 0 or (v and v < 64):
+        raise ValueError(f"{ROWS_ENV}={raw}: expected 0 (the lean rows) or at least 64")
+    return v
+
+
+def wait_ms() -> float:
+    raw = os.environ.get(WAIT_ENV, "").strip()
+    v = float(raw) if raw else 10.0
+    if v < 0:
+        raise ValueError(f"{WAIT_ENV}={raw}: expected 0 or more milliseconds")
+    return v
+
+
+ON = parse()
+
+
+def settings(lean_rows: int) -> list[int]:
+    """What both ranks must agree on: the knob and the group row budget."""
+
+    return [int(ON), limit(lean_rows) if ON else 0]
+
+
+def limit(lean_rows: int) -> int:
+    v = rows_env()
+    return min(v, lean_rows) if v else int(lean_rows)
+
+
+def kernels_ok() -> bool:
+    """No kernel of a fast chunk picks by the call's total rows: 0270's auto and 0260's once with a row threshold do
+    (same bits by their patches, but a group does not rely on it)."""
+
+    import sys
+
+    ex = sys.modules.get(__package__ + ".exl3_mm") if __package__ else None
+    if ex is None:
+        return True
+    return not getattr(ex, "AUTO", False) and not (getattr(ex, "ONCE", False) and getattr(ex, "ONCE_MIN_ROWS", 0))
+
+
+# -- rank 0: which pieces --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+def more_pieces(pieces: list[int], prefilling: Sequence[tuple[int, int, int]], allow: bool, piece: int,
+                rows_max: int) -> list[int]:
+    """This round's pieces with more of the waiting prompts' pieces when the fair share allows one: fewest tokens left
+    first, while the pieces' rows (at most ``piece`` each: an estimate, ``groups`` checks the real bounds) fit
+    ``rows_max``. ``prefilling``: (slot, tokens left, admission order), as ``batchplan.pick_pieces``."""
+
+    if not allow or rows_max <= 0:
+        return list(pieces)
+    left = {s: n for s, n, _ in prefilling}
+    out = list(pieces)
+    used = sum(min(left.get(s, piece), piece) for s in out)
+    for s, n, _ in sorted((p for p in prefilling if p[0] not in out), key=lambda p: (p[1], p[2], p[0])):
+        r = min(n, piece)
+        if used + r > rows_max:
+            break
+        out.append(s)
+        used += r
+    return out
+
+
+def coalesce(bat) -> None:
+    """Rank 0, ``Batcher._plan`` holding ``bat.cv``: when no slot holds a request and fewer requests wait than there
+    are slots, wait until ``bat.mpf_wait`` seconds after the oldest arrival (or until the slots are covered) so
+    requests that arrive together are admitted, and prefilled, together."""
+
+    import time
+
+    if not bat.queue or any(s is not None for s in bat.seqs):
+        return
+    now = time.perf_counter()
+    first = min((j.submitted or now) for j in bat.queue)
+    deadline = first + bat.mpf_wait
+    while len(bat.queue) < bat.n and not bat.stopping:
+        left = deadline - time.perf_counter()
+        if left <= 0:
+            break
+        bat.cv.wait(left)
+
+
+def pack(cands: Sequence[tuple[int, object, int] | tuple[int, None, int]], rows_max: int) -> list[list[int]]:
+    """Groups from (slot, key or None, rows) in round order: a member joins the open group of its key while the rows
+    fit, else opens a new one; None (ineligible) runs alone. Groups ordered by their first member."""
+
+    groups: list[list[int]] = []
+    rows: list[int] = []
+    open_: dict = {}
+    for slot, key, r in cands:
+        if key is None or r > rows_max:
+            groups.append([slot])
+            rows.append(r)
+            continue
+        i = open_.get(key)
+        if i is not None and rows[i] + r <= rows_max:
+            groups[i].append(slot)
+            rows[i] += r
+            continue
+        open_[key] = len(groups)
+        groups.append([slot])
+        rows.append(r)
+    return groups
+
+
+def piece_bounds(bat, slot: int) -> tuple[int, bool]:
+    """(the piece's end, whether 0335's solo rule could move it), under the request's knobs (``Batcher._piece``'s
+    arithmetic with the slots as they are now)."""
+
+    from . import batchplan, fastpf
+
+    e = bat.g.e
+    seq = bat.seqs[slot]
+    n = len(seq.job.prompt)
+    grid = batchplan.piece_grid(fastpf.grid(e.prefill_rows), int(getattr(e, "snap_grid", 0) or 0)) \
+        if e.fast_prefill else 0
+    others = [i for i, q in enumerate(bat.seqs) if q is not None and i != slot]
+    solo = batchplan.solo_piece(bat.solo, bat.piece, grid, others)
+    end = batchplan.piece_end(seq.done, n, solo, grid)
+    moves = bool(bat.solo and grid and batchplan.piece_end(seq.done, n, bat.piece, grid)
+                 != batchplan.piece_end(seq.done, n, bat.solo, grid))
+    return end, moves
+
+
+def engine_ok(e) -> bool:
+    """The engine prefills this request's knobs through a fast lean chunk (the only path grouped)."""
+
+    return bool(getattr(e, "fast_prefill", False)) and getattr(e, "lean", None) is not None
+
+
+def groups(bat, pieces: Sequence[int]) -> list[list[int]]:
+    """The round's pieces as groups (both ranks, the same result: from the slots' requests and ``rows_max``)."""
+
+    from . import dump as dump_mod, knobs, profile
+    from .vision_prep import has_vids
+
+    g = bat.g
+    rows_max = getattr(bat, "mpf_rows", 0) or 0
+    if len(pieces) < 2 or rows_max <= 0 or profile.ON or dump_mod.DUMP is not None or not kernels_ok():
+        return [[s] for s in pieces]
+    cands = []
+    for s in pieces:
+        seq = bat.seqs[s]
+        job = seq.job
+        key, rows = None, 0
+        if not has_vids(job.prompt) and seq.stepper is None:
+            with g._knobs(job.values):
+                if engine_ok(g.e):
+                    end, _ = piece_bounds(bat, s)
+                    rows = end - seq.done
+                    if 0 < rows:
+                        key = tuple(int(job.values[k]) for k in knobs.HEADER)
+        cands.append((s, key, rows))
+    return pack(cands, rows_max)
+
+
+# -- the group's prefill (both ranks) -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+class _Member:
+    """One slot's prefill in a group: ``decode._prefill`` cut at its forwards (``setup``, then per chunk ``before`` /
+    the group forward / ``after``, then ``finish`` inside ``Batcher._piece``)."""
+
+    def __init__(self, bat, slot: int, end: int) -> None:
+        from . import pfgrid
+
+        seq = bat.seqs[slot]
+        job = seq.job
+        _, mtp, dflash = bat.g._drafters(job.code)
+        self.slot, self.seq, self.job = slot, seq, job
+        self.state = bat.states[slot]
+        self.group = 1
+        self.mtp = mtp
+        self.drafter = bat.drafters[slot] if dflash else None
+        self.prompt = list(job.prompt[:end])
+        n = len(job.prompt)
+        # ``Batcher._piece``: e.snap_before = n (draft requests, the rule on); ``_prefill`` applies it when len == n
+        self.before = bool(job.draft and pfgrid.before_end() and end == n)
+        self.marks = tuple(seq.marks)
+        self.resume = seq.resume
+        self.error: BaseException | None = None
+        self.k = 0
+        self.last = None
+        self.last_hidden = None
+        self.view = None
+
+    # decode._prefill up to its chunk loop
+    def setup(self, e) -> None:
+        from . import b12xpf, fp8pf, pfglue, pfgrid
+        from .decode import absorb, restore
+
+        prompt = self.prompt
+        w, st = e.w, e.st
+        drafter = self.drafter
+        self.use_mtp = use_mtp = self.mtp and w.mtp is not None
+        fast = True
+        lean = getattr(e, "lean", None)
+        fp8pf.ON = fast and bool(getattr(e, "fp8_prefill", False))
+        grid = getattr(e, "snap_grid", None) or pfgrid.snapshot_grid()
+        self.tag = pfgrid.tag(fast, fp8pf.ON, grid, pfglue.latent_tc(getattr(e, "w", None)),
+                              b12xpf.tag_bits(getattr(e, "w", None)))
+        cap = lean.rows if lean is not None else e.rows
+        self.mtp_lo = pfglue.mtp_start(len(prompt)) if use_mtp else 0
+        self.fast_snap = None
+        self.mark_snaps: list = []
+        begin = 0
+        resume = self.resume
+        if resume is None:
+            e.reset()
+            if drafter is not None:
+                drafter.reset()
+        else:
+            begin = len(resume.ids)
+            if begin >= len(prompt) or list(prompt[:begin]) != resume.ids:
+                raise ValueError("a resumed prefill needs a snapshot of a strict prefix of the prompt")
+            if (use_mtp and resume.mtp_len < 0) or (drafter is not None and resume.drafter_end != begin):
+                raise ValueError("this snapshot's draft caches do not fit the request")
+            if not pfgrid.resumable(resume.grid, self.tag, begin):
+                raise ValueError(f"a snapshot of grid {resume.grid} at {begin} cannot resume a prefill of grid "
+                                 f"{self.tag}")
+            restore(e, resume, drafter)
+            if use_mtp:
+                k = resume.pending.shape[0]
+                pfglue.absorb(e, resume.pending, list(prompt[begin - k + 1:begin + 1]), begin - k, self.mtp_lo, absorb)
+        n = len(prompt)
+        self.begin, self.n = begin, n
+        self.step = pfgrid.chunk_rows(e.prefill_rows, n - begin, cap, fast)
+        self.plan = pl = pfgrid.plan(begin, n, self.step, fast=fast, marks=self.marks or (), grid=grid,
+                                     tail=getattr(e, "snap_tail", None), before=self.before)
+        if pl.snap == begin and resume is not None:
+            self.fast_snap = resume
+        # patches/0550 when present: the prefill selection's scratch sized before the first forward, as ``_prefill``
+        sparse = sys.modules.get(__package__ + ".sparse")
+        reserve = getattr(sparse, "reserve_for_prefill", None)
+        if reserve is not None and getattr(st, "index", None) is not None \
+                and n - 1 >= getattr(w.cfg, "dense_limit", n) and getattr(sparse, "SELECT", "") == "blocked":
+            reserve(begin, n, e.buf.rows if lean is not None else self.step, st.index[0][2], w.device)
+        room(w, st, n - begin, begin)            # every chunk's room (and 0290's pages) before any group forward
+
+    def span(self) -> tuple[int, int]:
+        return self.plan.spans[self.k]
+
+    def done(self) -> bool:
+        return self.k >= len(self.plan.spans)
+
+    def before_chunk(self, e) -> list[int]:
+        """Marks and the snapshot at the chunk's start; -> the chunk's tokens."""
+
+        from .decode import take_snapshot
+
+        start, stop = self.span()
+        pl, use_mtp = self.plan, self.use_mtp
+        pend = self.last_hidden if use_mtp else None
+        if start in pl.marks:
+            self.mark_snaps.append(take_snapshot(e, self.prompt[:start], pend, mtp=use_mtp, drafter=self.drafter,
+                                                 grid=self.tag, mtp_len=start - 1))
+        if start == pl.snap and start > self.begin:
+            self.fast_snap = take_snapshot(e, self.prompt[:start], pend, mtp=use_mtp, drafter=self.drafter,
+                                           grid=self.tag, mtp_len=start - 1)
+        return self.prompt[start:stop]
+
+    def after_chunk(self, e, logits, view) -> None:
+        """The chunk's rows are in (``view``: its final-normed rows and taps); ``decode._prefill``'s steps after the
+        forward, then the commit (``commit_member``)."""
+
+        from . import pfglue
+        from .decode import absorb, take_snapshot
+
+        start, stop = self.span()
+        R = stop - start
+        self.view = view
+        if hasattr(e, "rows_from"):
+            e.rows_from = view
+        self.last = logits.clone()
+        self.last_hidden = e.main_hidden(slice(R - 1, R)).clone()
+        if self.use_mtp:
+            nxt = list(self.prompt[start + 1:start + R + 1])
+            if nxt:
+                pfglue.absorb(e, e.main_hidden(slice(0, len(nxt))), nxt, start, self.mtp_lo, absorb)
+        if self.drafter is not None:
+            self.drafter.add_taps(e.tap_rows(R))
+        commit_member(e, self)
+        self.k += 1
+        if self.done() and self.plan.snap == self.n:       # the prompt (piece) ends on the grid
+            self.fast_snap = take_snapshot(e, self.prompt, self.last_hidden if self.use_mtp else None,
+                                           mtp=self.use_mtp, drafter=self.drafter, grid=self.tag)
+
+    def finish(self, e, prompt, sampling, *, mtp=True, drafter=None, resume=None) -> int:
+        """``decode.prefill``'s place in ``Batcher._piece``: the engine fields a prefill leaves, the first token."""
+
+        if self.error is not None:
+            raise self.error
+        if len(prompt) != len(self.prompt):
+            raise RuntimeError(f"multi prefill: slot {self.slot}'s piece ends at {len(prompt)}, the group ran it to "
+                               f"{len(self.prompt)}")
+        if not self.done():
+            raise RuntimeError(f"multi prefill: slot {self.slot}'s prefill did not finish")
+        e.fast_snap = self.fast_snap
+        e.mark_snaps = list(self.mark_snaps)
+        e.last_hidden = self.last_hidden
+        e.fast_rows = self.step
+        e.snap_before = 0
+        if hasattr(e, "rows_from"):
+            e.rows_from = self.view
+        self.seq.job.stats["multi_prefill"] = self.group
+        return e.sample(self.last, [len(self.prompt)], sampling)[0]
+
+
+def room(w, st, R: int, pos: int) -> None:
+    """``forward.check_room`` (the tests' fake models replace it)."""
+
+    from .forward import check_room
+
+    check_room(w, st, R, pos)
+
+
+def _failed(exc: BaseException):
+    def raise_(*a, **k):
+        raise exc
+
+    return raise_
+
+
+def run(bat, slots: Sequence[int]) -> None:
+    """The group's prefill up to each member's first token: every member's setup, then its chunks in lockstep (one
+    group forward per chunk index), each member's steps in slot order. Each member's piece then finishes in
+    ``Batcher._piece`` (``take``). A request's own error (ValueError, before any forward) makes its piece fail there,
+    as alone."""
+
+    g = bat.g
+    e = g.e
+    _done(bat).clear()                  # nothing left from an earlier round (every member's ``_piece`` takes its own)
+    job0 = bat.seqs[slots[0]].job
+    ends = {}
+    members: list[_Member] = []
+    with g._knobs(job0.values):
+        bounds = {s: piece_bounds(bat, s) for s in slots}
+    # ``_piece`` recomputes a member's bound when its turn comes: the members after it still hold their slots (no solo
+    # piece), but the LAST one may find every other slot freed (members done at their first token) and, with
+    # GLM53_TF_SOLO_PIECE, a bound the group did not run: it prefills alone then, unless another request holds a slot
+    slots = list(slots)
+    if bounds[slots[-1]][1] and not any(q is not None and i not in slots for i, q in enumerate(bat.seqs)):
+        slots.pop()
+    if len(slots) < 2:
+        return
+    with g._knobs(job0.values), _borrow_all(bat, slots):
+        for s in slots:
+            ends[s] = bounds[s][0]
+        for s in slots:
+            m = _Member(bat, s, ends[s])
+            m.group = len(slots)
+            with bat._on(s):
+                try:
+                    m.setup(e)
+                except ValueError as exc:
+                    _done(bat)[s] = _failed(exc)
+                    continue
+            members.append(m)
+        while True:
+            live = [m for m in members if not m.done()]
+            if not live:
+                break
+            chunks = []
+            for m in live:
+                with bat._on(m.slot):
+                    chunks.append(m.before_chunk(e))
+            logits, views = forward_group(e, live, chunks)
+            for i, m in enumerate(live):
+                with bat._on(m.slot):
+                    m.after_chunk(e, logits[i:i + 1], views[i])
+        bat.counts["multi_groups"] += 1
+        bat.counts["multi_members"] += len(members)
+    for m in members:
+        _done(bat)[m.slot] = m.finish
+
+
+def _done(bat) -> dict:
+    return bat.__dict__.setdefault("_mpf_done", {})
+
+
+def take(bat, slot: int):
+    """``Batcher._piece``: the group's result for ``slot`` (a ``decode.prefill`` stand-in), else None."""
+
+    done = bat.__dict__.get("_mpf_done")
+    return done.pop(slot, None) if done else None
+
+
+@contextlib.contextmanager
+def _borrow_all(bat, slots):
+    with contextlib.ExitStack() as stack:
+        for s in slots:
+            stack.enter_context(bat._borrow(s))
+        yield
+
+
+# -- the forward (hooks: the tests' fake models replace these) --------------------------------------------------------
+def forward_group(e, live: Sequence[_Member], chunks: Sequence[list[int]]):
+    """One forward over the members' chunks: -> (last-row logits [k, V/world], per member its rows' view)."""
+
+    w, b, lb = e.w, e.buf, e.lean
+    segs = []
+    off = 0
+    tokens: list[int] = []
+    tails = _tails(lb, len(live))
+    for i, (m, ch) in enumerate(zip(live, chunks)):
+        st = m.state
+        segs.append(Seg(st, off, len(ch), st.pos, tails[i], lb))
+        tokens += ch
+        off += len(ch)
+    stage(w, lb, segs, tokens)
+    logits = compute(w, b, lb, segs)
+    views = [SimpleNamespace(fnormed=lb.fnormed[s.off:s.off + s.R],
+                             tapcat=lb.tapcat[s.off:s.off + s.R] if lb.tapcat is not None else None) for s in segs]
+    for m, s in zip(live, segs):
+        m.seg = s
+    return logits, views
+
+
+def commit_member(e, m: _Member) -> None:
+    from . import lean
+
+    s = m.seg
+    lean.commit(e.w, s.st, SimpleNamespace(tail=s.tail), s.R)
+
+
+def stage(w, lb, segs, tokens: list[int]) -> None:
+    """The group's token ids into the lean set (one copy), each member's room checked at its position."""
+
+    from .forward import check_room
+
+    T = len(tokens)
+    if T > lb.rows:
+        raise RuntimeError(f"multi prefill: {T} rows, the lean buffers hold {lb.rows}")
+    for s in segs:
+        check_room(w, s.st, s.R, s.pos)
+    if lb.staged is not None:
+        lb.staged.synchronize()
+    lb.ids_host[:T].numpy()[:] = tokens
+    lb.ids[:T].copy_(lb.ids_host[:T], non_blocking=True)
+    if lb.staged is not None:
+        lb.staged.record()
+
+
+def _tails(lb, k: int):
+    """k KDA conv carries (``LeanBuffers.tail``'s shape each), kept on the lean set (not a tensor attribute: the set's
+    byte count stays the lean set's)."""
+
+    import torch
+
+    have = getattr(lb, "mpf_tails", None)           # a tuple: ``LeanBuffers.nbytes`` counts tensor attributes only
+    if have is None or have[0].shape[0] < k:
+        have = (torch.zeros((max(k, 4),) + tuple(lb.tail.shape), dtype=lb.tail.dtype, device=lb.tail.device),)
+        lb.mpf_tails = have
+    return [have[0][i] for i in range(k)]
+
+
+class Seg:
+    """A member's rows in a group forward: its State, first row in the lean set, rows, position, conv carry."""
+
+    __slots__ = ("st", "off", "R", "pos", "tail", "carry")
+
+    def __init__(self, st, off: int, R: int, pos: int, tail, lb) -> None:
+        self.st, self.off, self.R, self.pos, self.tail = st, off, R, pos, tail
+        # what ``lean._kda_block`` / ``_carry`` read of the lean set: the conv tail (the member's) and the state copy
+        self.carry = SimpleNamespace(tail=tail, rec_tmp=lb.rec_tmp)
+
+
+def blocks(segs: Sequence[Seg], block: int) -> list[tuple[int, int, int]]:
+    """(first row, rows, member) of every sub-block: each member's rows cut at ``block`` from its own start."""
+
+    out = []
+    for i, s in enumerate(segs):
+        for la in range(0, s.R, block):
+            out.append((s.off + la, min(block, s.R - la), i))
+    return out
+
+
+class _SegLB:
+    """The lean set as the chunk loops see it, with the group's sub-blocks (attribute reads and writes go to the set)."""
+
+    def __init__(self, lb, bl) -> None:
+        object.__setattr__(self, "_lb", lb)
+        object.__setattr__(self, "_bl", [(a, r) for a, r, _ in bl])
+
+    def __getattr__(self, name):
+        return getattr(object.__getattribute__(self, "_lb"), name)
+
+    def __setattr__(self, name, value) -> None:
+        setattr(object.__getattribute__(self, "_lb"), name, value)
+
+    def sub_blocks(self, R: int):
+        return list(object.__getattribute__(self, "_bl"))
+
+
+def _fxs_rows(lb, w):
+    from . import pfpp
+
+    return pfpp._fxs_rows(lb, w)
+
+
+def split_applies(w, lb, T: int) -> bool:
+    """0320's row split for a group of T rows: when the lone rule splits a chunk of T rows (more than one sub-block)."""
+
+    from . import pfpp
+
+    return (pfpp.ON and w.comm is not None and w.world == 2 and getattr(w.comm, "world", 2) == 2
+            and -(-T // lb.block) >= pfpp.MIN_BLOCKS)
+
+
+def compute(w, b, lb, segs: Sequence[Seg], *, head: bool = True):
+    """The group forward on staged rows (``stage``): -> the members' last-row logits [k, V/world] (a view of
+    ``b.logits``); every member's final-normed rows in ``lb.fnormed`` and taps in ``lb.tapcat`` at its rows. States
+    are committed by ``lean.commit`` per member (its ``Seg.tail``)."""
+
+    from . import lean, pfoverlap
+
+    T = sum(s.R for s in segs)
+    if T > lb.rows:
+        raise ValueError(f"multi prefill: {T} rows, the lean buffers hold {lb.rows}")
+    if lb.block > b.rows:
+        raise ValueError(f"lean sub-blocks of {lb.block} rows, the main buffers hold {b.rows}")
+    if len(segs) > b.logits.shape[0]:
+        raise ValueError(f"multi prefill: {len(segs)} members, {b.logits.shape[0]} logits rows")
+    bl = blocks(segs, lb.block)
+    with lean.chunk_rows(w, T):
+        if pfoverlap.on():
+            fxs = _pipelined(w, b, lb, segs, bl, T)
+        else:
+            fxs = _plain(w, b, lb, segs, bl, T)
+        from . import fastpf, qmm
+
+        with fastpf.chunk(b, w.head):
+            if head:
+                for i, s in enumerate(segs):
+                    r = s.off + s.R
+                    qmm.matmul(lb.fnormed[r - 1:r], w.head, fxs[r - 1:r], out=b.logits[i:i + 1], part=b.sk)
+            lean._join(w)
+    return b.logits[:len(segs)]
+
+
+def _attn_half(layer, w, s: Seg, b, lb, a: int, r: int) -> None:
+    """``lean._attn_half`` for the member's sub-block [a, a + r) (its local row a - off, its position)."""
+
+    from . import glue, lean
+    from .attention import CHUNK
+
+    c = w.cfg
+    la = a - s.off
+    pos = s.pos + la
+    x = lb.x[a:a + r]
+    h = layer.attn_hc
+    glue.hc_pre(x, h.fn, h.base, h.scale, layer.in_norm, b.normed[:r], b.xs[:r], b.post[:r], b.comb[:r],
+                b.hcpart[:r], c.eps, c.hc_eps, c.hc_iters)
+    b.site = (layer.index, "a")
+    st = s.st
+    if layer.kind == "kda":
+        g = lean._kda_block(layer, w, st, b, s.carry, la, r, pos)
+    else:
+        di = st.dsa_index[layer.index]
+        lb.pos_dev.fill_(pos)
+        g = lean.dsa_block(layer, w, st.kc[di], st.vc[di], lb.pos_dev, b, r, -(-(pos + r) // CHUNK),
+                           st.index[di] if st.index is not None else None, pos, None)
+    glue.hc_post(x, x, g, b.post[:r], b.comb[:r])
+
+
+def _plain(w, b, lb, segs, bl, T: int):
+    """0082's loop (``lean._compute``) over the group's sub-blocks. -> the final norm's group sums of every row."""
+
+    from . import fastpf, glue, lean
+
+    c = w.cfg
+    seg = _SegLB(lb, bl)
+    fxs = _fxs_rows(lb, w)
+    with fastpf.chunk(b, w.head):
+        glue.embed(lb.ids[:T], w.embed, c.hidden, c.streams, lb.x[:T])
+        for layer in w.layers:
+            for a, r, i in bl:
+                _attn_half(layer, w, segs[i], b, lb, a, r)
+            if layer.mlp is not None:
+                for a, r, _ in bl:
+                    lean._ffn_dense(layer, w, b, lb, a, r)
+            else:
+                lean._ffn_moe(layer, w, b, seg, T)
+            for slot in b.tap_at.get(layer.index, ()):
+                for a, r, _ in bl:
+                    glue.stream_mean(lb.x[a:a + r], b.taps[slot][:r])
+                    lb.tapcat[a:a + r, slot * lb.D:(slot + 1) * lb.D].copy_(b.taps[slot][:r])
+        for a, r, _ in bl:
+            glue.stream_mean(lb.x[a:a + r], b.hidden[:r])
+            glue.rmsnorm(b.hidden[:r], w.norm, c.eps, lb.fnormed[a:a + r], fxs[a:a + r])
+    return fxs
+
+
+def _seg_classes():
+    from . import glue, pfoverlap, pfpp
+
+    class _SegMixin:
+        """The member-aware attention piece: the sub-block's member, local row and position."""
+
+        def seg_setup(self, segs, bl) -> None:
+            self.segs = segs
+            self.owner = {a: i for a, _, i in bl}
+
+        def attn_pre(self, layer, a: int, r: int):
+            need = getattr(self, "need", None)
+            if need is not None:                 # 0320: the sub-block's shared rows first
+                need(a)
+            from . import lean
+            from .attention import CHUNK
+
+            s = self.segs[self.owner[a]]
+            w, b, lb = self.w, self.b, self.lb
+            la = a - s.off
+            pos = s.pos + la
+            st = s.st
+            b.site = (layer.index, "a")
+            if layer.kind == "kda":
+                return lean._kda_block(layer, w, st, b, s.carry, la, r, pos, lb.normed[a:a + r], lb.xs[a:a + r])
+            b.normed[:r].copy_(lb.normed[a:a + r])
+            b.xs[:r].copy_(lb.xs[a:a + r])
+            di = st.dsa_index[layer.index]
+            lb.pos_dev.fill_(pos)
+            return lean.dsa_block(layer, w, st.kc[di], st.vc[di], lb.pos_dev, b, r, -(-(pos + r) // CHUNK),
+                                  st.index[di] if st.index is not None else None, pos, None)
+
+    class _MultiChunk(_SegMixin, pfoverlap._Chunk):
+        """0084's pipelined chunk over the group's sub-blocks; the final norm's group sums kept for every row (each
+        member's head reads its last row's)."""
+
+        def ffn_post(self, layer, nxt, a: int, r: int, g) -> None:
+            if nxt is not None:
+                return super().ffn_post(layer, nxt, a, r, g)
+            w, b, lb, c = self.w, self.b, self.lb, self.c
+            taps = b.tap_at.get(layer.index, ())
+            for s0, n in self.slabs(a, r):
+                x = lb.x[s0:s0 + n]
+                self.hc_post(g, a, s0, n)
+                for slot in taps:
+                    glue.stream_mean(x, b.taps[slot][:n])
+                    lb.tapcat[s0:s0 + n, slot * lb.D:(slot + 1) * lb.D].copy_(b.taps[slot][:n])
+                glue.stream_mean(x, b.hidden[:n])
+                glue.rmsnorm(b.hidden[:n], w.norm, c.eps, lb.fnormed[s0:s0 + n], self.fxs[s0:s0 + n])
+
+    class _MultiSplit(_SegMixin, pfpp._SplitChunk):
+        """0320's row-split chunk over the group's sub-blocks (its final sums are per row already)."""
+
+    return _MultiChunk, _MultiSplit
+
+
+_CLASSES = None
+
+
+def classes():
+    global _CLASSES
+    if _CLASSES is None:
+        _CLASSES = _seg_classes()
+    return _CLASSES
+
+
+def _pipelined(w, b, lb, segs, bl, T: int):
+    from . import fastpf, pfoverlap, pfpp
+
+    Multi, Split = classes()
+    seg = _SegLB(lb, bl)
+    mode = pfoverlap.MODE
+    split = split_applies(w, lb, T)
+    if split:
+        pipe = pfpp._pipe(w, lb)
+        cls = Split
+    else:
+        pipe = pfoverlap._pipe(w, b, lb)
+        cls = Multi
+    pipe.begin(mode.gather)
+    run = cls(w, segs[0].st, b, seg, T, pipe, pfoverlap.slab_rows(w, lb.block) if mode.slab else 0)
+    run.seg_setup(segs, bl)
+    if not split:
+        run.fxs = _fxs_rows(lb, w)
+    with fastpf.chunk(b, w.head):
+        b.defer = pipe
+        ok = False
+        try:
+            run.run()
+            ok = True
+        finally:
+            b.defer = None
+            if not ok:
+                if split:
+                    run.rows_pending.clear()
+                pipe.abort()
+        if not pipe.idle() or (split and run.rows_pending):
+            raise RuntimeError("multi prefill: exchanges left pending at the end of a group forward")
+    compute.last = run                    # tests: the piece order
+    return run.fxs
+
+
+compute.last = None
diff --git a/src/tensorfold/families/glm5_next/spark/mtp.py b/src/tensorfold/families/glm5_next/spark/mtp.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..c5444ab
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/tensorfold/families/glm5_next/spark/mtp.py
@@ -0,0 +1,92 @@
+"""GLM-5.3-Flash's MTP head (the nextn layer) on CUDA, through the same row-invariant kernels as the model.
+
+At position i it reads the main model's hidden row h_i and the embedding of token i + 1, the way vLLM's GLM-5.3
+MTP reads them: h is the final-normed row, chained drafts recycle the head's shared_head.norm output, and the
+embedding at position 0 is zeroed (the final-normed row predicted the next token 0.739 of the time against 0.696
+for the mean of the streams before the final norm):
+
+    x = eh_proj([enorm(embed(t_{i+1})) | hnorm(h_i)])
+    x = x + attn(input_layernorm(x))            DSA over the head's own cache, plain residual (no hyper-connections)
+    x = x + moe(post_attention_layernorm(x))
+    logits = lm_head(shared_head.norm(x))
+
+Its output x feeds the next chained draft as h. The head's attention cache holds one entry per absorbed
+position (``State.mtp_len``); chained drafts append entries that the next absorb trims.
+"""
+
+from __future__ import annotations
+
+from typing import Sequence
+
+import torch
+
+from . import draftvocab, glue, profile, qmm
+from .forward import Buffers, State, _join, check_room, dsa_block, moe_block
+from .weights import Weights
+
+
+def mtp_stage(w: Weights, st: State, b: Buffers, next_tokens: Sequence[int], hidden: torch.Tensor) -> int:
+    """Host work before an MTP step: the next tokens and the input hidden rows into the static buffers."""
+
+    n = len(next_tokens)
+    b.zero_first = st.mtp_len == 0
+    check_room(w, st, n, pos=st.mtp_len)
+    b.staged.synchronize()
+    b.ids_host[:n].numpy()[:] = list(next_tokens)
+    b.ids[:n].copy_(b.ids_host[:n], non_blocking=True)
+    if hidden.data_ptr() != b.hin.data_ptr():
+        b.hin[:n].copy_(hidden)
+    b.staged.record()
+    return n
+
+
+def mtp_compute(w: Weights, st: State, b: Buffers, n: int, *, last_only: bool = True,
+                nch: int | None = None, host_pos: int | None = None, npb: int | None = None,
+                full: bool = False) -> torch.Tensor:
+    """The MTP head's GPU work on staged rows (capturable; ``npb``: patches/0050's long-context step). patches/0420:
+    the logits of the listed rows only (``draftvocab``) unless ``full``."""
+
+    c = w.cfg
+    m = w.mtp
+    D = c.hidden
+    glue.embed(b.ids[:n], w.embed, D, 1, b.me[:n])
+    if b.zero_first:
+        b.me[0].zero_()
+    glue.rmsnorm(b.me[:n], m.enorm, c.eps, b.mcat[:n, :D])
+    glue.rmsnorm(b.hin[:n], m.hnorm, c.eps, b.mcat[:n, D:])
+    qmm.matmul(b.mcat[:n], m.eh, qmm.group_sums(b.mcat[:n], b.mxs[:n]), out=b.mx[:n], part=b.sk)
+    layer = m.layer
+    glue.rmsnorm(b.mx[:n], layer.in_norm, c.eps, b.normed[:n], b.xs[:n])
+    if profile.ON:
+        profile.lap("misc")
+    b.site = ("mtp", "a")
+    g = dsa_block(layer, w, st.mtp_kc, st.mtp_vc, st.mtp_pos_dev, b, n, nch,
+                  st.index[-1] if st.index is not None else None, host_pos, npb)
+    glue.residual_add(b.mx[:n], b.mx[:n], g)
+    glue.rmsnorm(b.mx[:n], layer.post_norm, c.eps, b.normed[:n], b.xs[:n])
+    b.site = ("mtp", "f")
+    g = moe_block(layer, w, b, n)
+    glue.residual_add(b.mx[:n], b.mx[:n], g)
+    lo = n - 1 if last_only else 0
+    k = n - lo
+    glue.rmsnorm(b.mx[lo:n], m.norm, c.eps, b.fnormed[:k], b.fxs[:k])
+    head = draftvocab.head_for(w, "mtp", full)       # the head's logits only draft (patches/0420: listed rows)
+    out = qmm.matmul(b.fnormed[:k], head, b.fxs[:k], out=b.logits[:k, :head.n], part=b.sk)
+    if profile.ON:
+        profile.lap("head")
+    _join(w)
+    return out
+
+
+@torch.no_grad()
+def mtp_forward(w: Weights, st: State, b: Buffers, next_tokens: Sequence[int], hidden: torch.Tensor,
+                *, last_only: bool = True, full: bool = False) -> torch.Tensor:
+    """Rows (hidden [n, D] bf16, the tokens after them): logits of the last row [1, V/world] (or all rows), with
+    the head's output rows in b.mx[:n]. Writes n entries at the head's cache slots mtp_len.. (the caller
+    advances ``st.mtp_len``)."""
+
+    n = mtp_stage(w, st, b, next_tokens, hidden)
+    from .attention import CHUNK
+
+    return mtp_compute(w, st, b, n, last_only=last_only, nch=-(-(st.mtp_len + n) // CHUNK), host_pos=st.mtp_len,
+                       full=full)
diff --git a/src/tensorfold/families/glm5_next/spark/mtpw.py b/src/tensorfold/families/glm5_next/spark/mtpw.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..93e70e5
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/tensorfold/families/glm5_next/spark/mtpw.py
@@ -0,0 +1,87 @@
+"""patches/0430, GLM53_TF_MTP_WEIGHTS=<dir>: serve a distilled MTP head (``train/mtp_distill.py``'s export) in place of
+the checkpoint's own. Off (unset / empty / 0): ``weights.load`` exactly as before.
+
+The folder holds full, unsplit BF16 tensors under the checkpoint's own names (``*.safetensors``), only for the MTP
+layer (``model.language_model.layers.<num_hidden_layers>.*``: attention, eh_proj, norms, router, shared expert). Each
+replaces the checkpoint's tensor of that name; this rank's part is sliced by the checkpoint's own split rules
+(``split.rule``) and stored the way the engine stores the checkpoint's (GLM53_TF_NONEXPERT: q4mse in production), so
+the exported BF16 weights go through the same quantization at load that training emulated. The routed experts stay
+the checkpoint's (EXL3).
+
+It lives outside ``weights.py`` so the prepared folders of patches/0140 (keyed by a digest of ``weights.py``) stay
+valid when the knob is off; with the knob on, the folder's files join the prepared tree's key (another head is
+another tree)."""
+
+from __future__ import annotations
+
+import os
+from pathlib import Path
+
+
+def mtp_weights_dir() -> str:
+    v = os.environ.get("GLM53_TF_MTP_WEIGHTS", "").strip()
+    return "" if v.lower() in ("", "0", "off") else v
+
+
+class _Overlay:
+    """A ``split.RankReader`` whose MTP-layer tensors come from the override folder when it has them."""
+
+    def __init__(self, base, over, prefix: str) -> None:
+        self.base, self.over, self.prefix = base, over, prefix
+        self.names = set(over.index)
+        bad = sorted(n for n in self.names if not n.startswith(prefix))
+        if bad:
+            raise ValueError(f"GLM53_TF_MTP_WEIGHTS may only replace MTP-layer tensors ({prefix}*); found {bad[:3]}")
+        self.used: set[str] = set()
+
+    def get(self, name: str):
+        if name in self.names:
+            self.used.add(name)
+            return self.over.get(name)
+        return self.base.get(name)
+
+    def __getattr__(self, name):
+        return getattr(self.base, name)
+
+
+def load(model_dir, *, rank: int, device: str = "cuda"):
+    """``weights.load`` with the MTP layer's tensors replaced from GLM53_TF_MTP_WEIGHTS (when set)."""
+
+    from . import fastboot, split, weights
+
+    where = mtp_weights_dir()
+    if not where:
+        return weights.load(model_dir, rank=rank, device=device)
+
+    def build():
+        cfg = weights.Config.read(model_dir)
+        if not cfg.mtp_layers:
+            raise ValueError("GLM53_TF_MTP_WEIGHTS: this checkpoint has no MTP layer")
+        prefix = weights.PREFIX + f"layers.{cfg.layers}."
+        orig = split.RankReader
+        made: list[_Overlay] = []
+
+        def reader(d, r):
+            o = _Overlay(orig(d, r), orig(where, r), prefix)
+            made.append(o)
+            return o
+
+        split.RankReader = reader            # ``load_checkpoint`` imports it at call time
+        try:
+            w = weights.load_checkpoint(model_dir, rank=rank, device=device)
+        finally:
+            split.RankReader = orig
+        ov = made[0]
+        missing = sorted(ov.names - ov.used)
+        if missing:
+            raise ValueError(f"GLM53_TF_MTP_WEIGHTS: tensors the engine does not read: {missing[:5]}")
+        if rank == 0:
+            print(f"[tensorfold] MTP head (patches/0430): {len(ov.used)} tensors from {where}", flush=True)
+        w.meta["mtp_weights"] = str(where)
+        return w
+
+    if fastboot.prepared_root() is None:
+        return build()
+    extra = {"mtp_weights": [str(Path(where).resolve()), fastboot.files_ident(where)]}
+    return fastboot.cached_tree("weights", fastboot.weights_key(model_dir, rank, device=device, extra=extra), build,
+                                device)
diff --git a/src/tensorfold/families/glm5_next/spark/overlap.py b/src/tensorfold/families/glm5_next/spark/overlap.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..859b701
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/tensorfold/families/glm5_next/spark/overlap.py
@@ -0,0 +1,206 @@
+"""GLM53_TF_COMM: what the engine does around its cross-rank all-gathers (default: nothing, upstream behaviour).
+
+Every block of a layer ends in an all-gather of fp32 partials (``forward.gather``), and the next kernel needs the
+gathered row: the hyper-connection epilogue, the next mix and RMSNorm read the whole row, so no work of the model
+can run beside the exchange and no two exchanges can be merged. At one to eight rows an exchange carries 16 to
+128 KiB a rank and takes about 28 us inside a CUDA graph, almost all of it latency, while the GPU's memory system
+sits idle. The variants use that time, or shorten it, without changing a bit of any result:
+
+- ``prefetch[:MB]``: while the all-gather runs, a side stream reads the first MB (default 4) of the weights the
+  next kernels read (the next mix's ``fn``, the router, the shared expert's gate/up, the next layer's attention
+  projection, the head) into L2, so those kernels find them there. Loads only, into a dummy sink: every kernel
+  of the model runs unchanged, on the same inputs, in the same order (the EXL3 shared expert, independent of the
+  routed ones, is computed before them so its prefetched rows are still in L2). Captured in the step's CUDA
+  graph like the all-gather.
+- ``ll`` / ``ll128``: NCCL_PROTO=LL or LL128 for the communicator (unless NCCL_PROTO is set already). The
+  protocol only changes how bytes travel; an all-gather is a copy. Both ranks must use the same value.
+
+Variants combine with commas: ``GLM53_TF_COMM=prefetch:4,ll``. ``nccl`` or empty is upstream.
+"""
+
+from __future__ import annotations
+
+import os
+from dataclasses import dataclass
+
+import torch
+import triton
+import triton.language as tl
+
+ENV = "GLM53_TF_COMM"
+DEFAULT_PREFETCH_MB = 4.0
+
+
+@dataclass(frozen=True)
+class Variant:
+    prefetch_mb: float = 0.0          # 0: no prefetch
+    proto: str | None = None          # NCCL_PROTO to set, if any
+
+
+def variant(value: str | None = None) -> Variant:
+    raw = os.environ.get(ENV, "") if value is None else value
+    prefetch, proto = 0.0, None
+    for tok in (t.strip().lower() for t in raw.split(",")):
+        if tok in ("", "nccl", "default"):
+            continue
+        name, _, arg = tok.partition(":")
+        if name == "prefetch":
+            try:
+                prefetch = float(arg) if arg else DEFAULT_PREFETCH_MB
+            except ValueError:
+                raise ValueError(f"{ENV}: bad prefetch size {arg!r} (MB)") from None
+            if not 0 < prefetch <= 64:
+                raise ValueError(f"{ENV}: prefetch size must be in (0, 64] MB, got {arg}")
+        elif name in ("ll", "ll128") and not arg:
+            proto = "LL" if name == "ll" else "LL128"
+        else:
+            raise ValueError(f"{ENV}: unknown variant {tok!r} (nccl, prefetch[:MB], ll, ll128; comma-separated)")
+    return Variant(prefetch, proto)
+
+
+def nccl_env(v: Variant | None = None) -> None:
+    """Before the communicator is created (NCCL reads its environment once)."""
+
+    v = variant() if v is None else v
+    if v.proto is not None:
+        os.environ.setdefault("NCCL_PROTO", v.proto)
+
+
+# -- L2 prefetch ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+@triton.jit
+def _touch(P, SINK, n, BLOCK: tl.constexpr, PROGS: tl.constexpr):
+    """Read n int32 words (PROGS programs, BLOCK words at a time, strided) through L2; the sum goes to a sink so
+    the loads are kept. Writes nothing the model reads. ``.cg`` caches the lines in L2 only (bypassing L1); no
+    eviction hint: Triton's evict_last is an L1 hint, which ptxas rejects with ``.cg`` on sm_121a."""
+
+    pid = tl.program_id(0)
+    offs = tl.arange(0, BLOCK)
+    acc = tl.zeros((BLOCK,), dtype=tl.int32)
+    for start in range(pid * BLOCK, n, PROGS * BLOCK):
+        i = start + offs
+        acc += tl.load(P + i, mask=i < n, other=0, cache_modifier=".cg")
+    tl.store(SINK + pid, tl.sum(acc, axis=0))
+
+
+def _words(t: torch.Tensor, nbytes: int) -> torch.Tensor | None:
+    """The first nbytes of t (whole int32 words) as an int32 view of the same memory, or None."""
+
+    if not isinstance(t, torch.Tensor) or not t.is_cuda or not t.is_contiguous() or t.data_ptr() % 16:
+        return None
+    nbytes = min(nbytes, t.numel() * t.element_size()) // 16 * 16
+    if nbytes <= 0:
+        return None
+    return t.reshape(-1).view(torch.uint8)[:nbytes].view(torch.int32)
+
+
+def _mat(q) -> list[torch.Tensor]:
+    """A matrix's tensors in the order worth prefetching: the small per-group scales first, then the words."""
+
+    if q is None:
+        return []
+    if hasattr(q, "biases"):                        # qmm.Q4
+        return [q.scales, q.biases, q.weight]
+    if hasattr(q, "scales"):                        # qmm.Q8 (patches/0470)
+        return [q.scales, q.weight]
+    return [q.weight]                               # qmm.B16
+
+
+def _take(tensors: list, budget: int) -> list[torch.Tensor]:
+    out, left = [], budget
+    for t in tensors:
+        if left < 16:
+            break
+        v = _words(t, left)
+        if v is not None:
+            out.append(v)
+            left -= v.numel() * 4
+    return out
+
+
+def _ffn_reads(layer, with_hc: bool) -> list:
+    reads = [layer.ffn_hc.fn] if with_hc and layer.ffn_hc is not None else []
+    reads.append(layer.post_norm)
+    if layer.mlp is not None:
+        reads += _mat(layer.mlp.gu)
+    elif layer.moe is not None:
+        reads += [layer.moe.router, layer.moe.bias]
+        if layer.moe.shared is not None:
+            reads += _mat(layer.moe.shared.gu)
+    return reads
+
+
+def _attn_reads(layer) -> list:
+    reads = [layer.attn_hc.fn] if layer.attn_hc is not None else []
+    reads.append(layer.in_norm)
+    reads += _mat(layer.kda.proj if layer.kind == "kda" else layer.dsa.proj)
+    return reads
+
+
+def plans(w, budget: int) -> dict:
+    """Per all-gather site ((layer index, "a" | "f") and ("mtp", "a" | "f")): the int32 views to prefetch, the
+    weights the kernels after that all-gather read first, up to ``budget`` bytes."""
+
+    out = {}
+    layers = w.layers
+    for i, layer in enumerate(layers):
+        out[(layer.index, "a")] = _take(_ffn_reads(layer, True), budget)
+        nxt = _attn_reads(layers[i + 1]) if i + 1 < len(layers) else [w.norm] + _mat(w.head)
+        out[(layer.index, "f")] = _take(nxt, budget)
+    if w.mtp is not None:
+        out[("mtp", "a")] = _take(_ffn_reads(w.mtp.layer, False), budget)
+        from . import draftvocab
+
+        head = draftvocab.head_for(w, "mtp")         # patches/0420: the listed rows when the MTP head drafts over them
+        out[("mtp", "f")] = _take([w.mtp.norm] + _mat(head), budget)
+    return out
+
+
+class Prefetcher:
+    """Launches a site's prefetch on a side stream forked from the current stream (before the all-gather is
+    queued); ``join`` makes the current stream wait for the side stream (end of every forward, so a captured
+    graph has no open fork)."""
+
+    BLOCK = 2048
+
+    def __init__(self, w, mb: float) -> None:
+        dev = w.device
+        props = torch.cuda.get_device_properties(dev)
+        budget = int(mb * 2**20)
+        l2 = int(getattr(props, "L2_cache_size", 0) or 0)
+        if l2:
+            budget = min(budget, l2 // 2)            # leave room for what the kernels themselves keep in L2
+        self.budget = budget
+        self.progs = max(1, props.multi_processor_count // 2)   # the other half stays free for the all-gather
+        self.sink = torch.zeros((self.progs,), dtype=torch.int32, device=dev)
+        self.side = torch.cuda.Stream(device=dev)
+        self.plans = plans(w, budget)
+        self.pending = False
+        self.launches = 0
+
+    def launch(self, site, R: int | None = None) -> None:     # R: patches/0460's row limit (unused here)
+        segs = self.plans.get(site)
+        if not segs:
+            return
+        self.side.wait_stream(torch.cuda.current_stream())      # after the block's partials, beside the all-gather
+        with torch.cuda.stream(self.side):
+            for s in segs:
+                _touch[(self.progs,)](s, self.sink, s.numel(), BLOCK=self.BLOCK, PROGS=self.progs, num_warps=4)
+        self.pending = True
+        self.launches += 1
+
+    def join(self) -> None:
+        if self.pending:
+            torch.cuda.current_stream().wait_stream(self.side)
+            self.pending = False
+
+
+def install(w) -> Prefetcher | None:
+    """At engine build (before graph capture): the prefetcher on ``w.meta["prefetch"]`` when the variant asks
+    for one and there is a second rank to wait for."""
+
+    v = variant()
+    pf = None
+    if v.prefetch_mb > 0 and w.world > 1 and w.comm is not None and torch.cuda.is_available():
+        pf = Prefetcher(w, v.prefetch_mb)
+    w.meta["prefetch"] = pf
+    return pf
diff --git a/src/tensorfold/families/glm5_next/spark/pfglue.py b/src/tensorfold/families/glm5_next/spark/pfglue.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..2c64b5c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/tensorfold/families/glm5_next/spark/pfglue.py
@@ -0,0 +1,330 @@
+"""Prefill "glue" for GLM-5.3-Flash on CUDA (patches/0190): the small ops between the big matmuls that a fast 8,192-row
+chunk now spends most of its non-expert time in, each behind its own knob (per request through patches/0090's
+header, so one load can A/B them).
+
+Measured (28,045-token cold prompt, fast + lean 8,192-row chunks, fast2 experts, overlap, latent KV; 23.09 s):
+``moe.router`` 1,268 ms, ``hc`` 2,916 ms (with the gather waits the overlap moves there), ``mtp.*`` ~1,300 ms,
+``moe.combine`` 802, ``moe.shared`` 961.
+
+1. ``moe_glue`` (GLM53_TF_MOE_GLUE = bits, default 0), windows of 64+ rows (decode / verify windows and graph
+   captures keep the old kernels):
+   - bit 1: the MoE grouping by a stable sort and a scatter (``glue.group_sorted``) instead of ``glue._group``, one
+     program that walks the chunk's R x 9 picks twice and its R member columns twice (O(R) serial on one SM: ~5-8 ms
+     a MoE layer at 8,192 rows, estimated from the loop counts; most of ``moe.router``). The outputs are integers
+     equal element for element to ``_group``'s (ids, count, members);
+   - bit 2: the router's 8 K slices in one kernel (``glue._router_fused``: each slice's dot chain as before, the
+     slices added in order in registers; no [8, R, 288] fp32 partial buffer written and read back, 150 MB a layer
+     at 8,192 rows);
+   - bit 4: the combine reads the shared expert's fp32 output where its matmul wrote it (``glue._combine_s``)
+     instead of a copy in its slot of ``ey`` (32 KB a row a MoE layer of traffic).
+   Same bits in every case, so replies, snapshots and the session store do not depend on the knob.
+
+2. ``mtp_window`` (GLM53_TF_MTP_PREFILL_WINDOW = tokens, default 0 = off): a prefill of n tokens runs the MTP head
+   (one DSA + MoE layer, every position) only on positions p >= lo = (n - W) rounded down to a multiple of 64. For
+   positions below lo the head's caches (latent / K,V rows, its indexer's keys and gates, and the pools those rows
+   complete) are ZEROED and ``mtp_len`` advances as if absorbed. The MTP head only drafts: a draft is verified by the
+   main model's window, and the keyed sampler and commit decide every token, so replies are those of the full head
+   (drafted == serial holds for any draft source). What changes is which drafts are proposed, i.e. speed, never
+   the reply. Determinism: the skipped rows are zeros whatever ran before, so the head's caches after a prefill are
+   a function of (prompt, W, the resume point); a resumed prefill's head rows below its resume point are those the
+   earlier request wrote (its own n and W), so drafts (not replies) after a resume may differ from a fresh prefill's,
+   as patches/0065 already allows for the DFlash2 ring. ``lo`` depends on the prompt length only (not on C or the
+   chunking), so the fast rule's chunk-size independence (patches/0085) holds for the head's rows too.
+   Batch mode (patches/0120) prefills a prompt in pieces, each a prefill of a prefix: every piece keeps its own last
+   W positions, so the saving there is smaller (never a correctness issue).
+
+3. ``hc_fused`` (GLM53_TF_HC_FUSED = 0..3, default 0; fast chunks through patches/0084's pipeline): bit 0 runs
+   hc_post and the next hc_pre's 24 mixing dots + square sums as one kernel (``glue._hc_post_part``: the new streams
+   are fed from registers into the partial's tensor-core dots instead of being re-read, one launch fewer per slab);
+   bit 1 runs hc_pre's finish with its 16 partial loads unrolled (``glue._hc_finish_u``: all in flight at once, added
+   in the same block order; the per-row finish was a chain of 16 dependent L2 round trips). Same arithmetic as the
+   separate kernels, operation for operation; the GPU test checks the bits (a Triton reduction's order follows the
+   layout the compiler picks, so "same code, same shapes, same warps" is checked, not assumed). Row-independent
+   (per-row mixes; 64-row tiles of independent mma rows).
+
+4. ``attn_bm32`` (GLM53_TF_ATTN_BM32, default 0): bf16 fast chunks use the latent attention's 32-query tiles (all 32
+   local heads of a row in one tile: one gather of the row's selected latent rows instead of two), which FP8 fast
+   chunks already use (patches/0083). 0060 measured -24% a layer for 1024 sparse rows and identical bits to the
+   16-query tile; decode keeps 16 (1-4-row windows are faster with it). The fast rule does not need prefill bits to
+   equal decode bits (fastpf), only determinism and row independence, which a tile of one row's heads has. The knob
+   is per request only because the bits are the same (checked on the GPU): were they not, snapshots of the two
+   settings must not mix, and it would have to be a load-time switch.
+
+5. ``GLM53_TF_LATENT_TC=1`` (load-time, default 0; NEW arithmetic): bf16 fast chunks run the latent absorb / expand
+   on bf16 tensor cores (``latent.absorb_tc`` / ``expand_tc``, patches/0083's kernels, tested against float64 there)
+   instead of the fp32 FMA-pipe kernels, which are most of ``dsa.o_proj`` (1.9 s of a 28k prompt) and part of
+   ``dsa.proj``. The operands are rounded to bf16 at the dot (q, u and kv_b's dequantized tile; fp32 sums in the same
+   K order): the usual bf16 matmul precision, not FP8's e4m3. Fast replies change (like GLM53_TF_KDA_PROJ_BF16);
+   drafted == serial and resumed == fresh hold (deterministic, row-independent 64-row tiles), and its snapshots are
+   tagged G + 2 (``pfgrid.TC``) so no prefill resumes from the other arithmetic. Both ranks must agree (checked at
+   load). Off by default: it is the user's call whether bf16-level reply changes are acceptable (FP8 prefill was
+   rejected for its e4m3 divergence).
+
+Items 1, 3, 4 give the same bits; 2 changes the MTP head's rows only; 5 is new arithmetic (opt-in, load-time).
+"""
+
+from __future__ import annotations
+
+import os
+from typing import Sequence
+
+GROUP_ENV = "GLM53_TF_MOE_GLUE"
+MTP_ENV = "GLM53_TF_MTP_PREFILL_WINDOW"
+HC_ENV = "GLM53_TF_HC_FUSED"
+BM32_ENV = "GLM53_TF_ATTN_BM32"
+TC_ENV = "GLM53_TF_LATENT_TC"
+GRID = 64
+
+
+def _int_env(name: str, default: int) -> int:
+    raw = os.environ.get(name, "").strip()
+    if not raw:
+        return default
+    try:
+        v = int(raw)
+    except ValueError:
+        raise ValueError(f"{name}={raw!r}: expected an integer") from None
+    if v < 0:
+        raise ValueError(f"{name}={raw!r}: expected 0 or more")
+    return v
+
+
+def moe_glue_default() -> int:
+    """GLM53_TF_MOE_GLUE bits: 1 sorted grouping, 2 one-kernel router, 4 the combine reading the shared expert in
+    place (7 = all)."""
+
+    v = _int_env(GROUP_ENV, 0)
+    if v > 7:
+        raise ValueError(f"{GROUP_ENV}={v}: expected 0 to 7")
+    return v
+
+
+def group_default() -> bool:
+    return bool(moe_glue_default() & 1)
+
+
+def moe_glue(glue) -> int:
+    """The current ``moe_glue`` value from glue's switches."""
+
+    return int(bool(glue.GROUP_SORT)) | (2 if glue.ROUTER_FUSED else 0) | (4 if glue.SHARED_INPLACE else 0)
+
+
+def set_moe_glue(glue, v: int) -> None:
+    glue.GROUP_SORT = bool(v & 1)
+    glue.ROUTER_FUSED = bool(v & 2)
+    glue.SHARED_INPLACE = bool(v & 4)
+
+
+def mtp_window_default() -> int:
+    return _int_env(MTP_ENV, 0)
+
+
+def bm32_default() -> bool:
+    return bool(_int_env(BM32_ENV, 0))
+
+
+def hc_default() -> int:
+    """GLM53_TF_HC_FUSED: 0 off, 1 hc_post + the next hc_pre's partial dots in one kernel, 2 hc_pre's finish with its
+    loads unrolled, 3 both (fast chunks through 0084's pipeline only)."""
+
+    v = _int_env(HC_ENV, 0)
+    if v > 3:
+        raise ValueError(f"{HC_ENV}={v}: expected 0 to 3")
+    return v
+
+
+# what the next prefill runs (``tf_knobs.mtp_window`` switches it per request; both ranks, the header carries it)
+MTP_WINDOW = mtp_window_default()
+
+
+def mtp_start(n: int, window: int | None = None) -> int:
+    """The first position of an n-token prompt whose MTP row is computed: 0 (window off or the prompt fits), else
+    (n - window) rounded down to a multiple of 64 (so the zeroed pools are whole and the rule is a function of n)."""
+
+    window = MTP_WINDOW if window is None else window
+    if window <= 0 or n <= window:
+        return 0
+    return (n - window) // GRID * GRID
+
+
+def zero_mtp_rows(st, s: int, e: int) -> None:
+    """The MTP head's cache rows [s, e) (latent or K/V, its indexer's keys and gates) and the pools rows s..e-1
+    complete (p with s <= 4p + 3 < e) set to zero: what a skipped position leaves, whatever ran before."""
+
+    if e <= s:
+        return
+    kc = getattr(st, "mtp_kc", None)
+    if kc is None:
+        return
+    pages = getattr(st, "pages", None)
+    if pages is not None:                        # patches/0290: paged caches, zeroed page by page (mapped first)
+        pages.ensure(e)
+
+    def zero(t, a: int, b: int) -> None:
+        if getattr(t, "is_paged", False):
+            t.zero_rows(a, b)
+        else:
+            t[a:b].zero_()
+
+    zero(kc, s, e)
+    vc = getattr(st, "mtp_vc", None)
+    if vc is not None and vc is not kc:
+        zero(vc, s, e)
+    index = getattr(st, "index", None)
+    if index is not None:
+        ik, ig, pk = index[-1]
+        zero(ik, s, e)
+        zero(ig, s, e)
+        p0, p1 = s // 4, e // 4
+        if p1 > p0:
+            zero(pk, p0, p1)
+
+
+def absorb(e, hidden, next_tokens: Sequence[int], p0: int, lo: int, absorb_fn):
+    """``decode.absorb`` of rows at positions p0, p0 + 1, ... (hidden [k, D], the tokens after them), with the rows
+    below ``lo`` skipped: their head caches zeroed and ``mtp_len`` advanced past them. ``absorb_fn``: decode.absorb.
+    Returns the last absorbed row's logits (None when every row was skipped; prefill does not read them).
+    With ``MTP_CACHE`` (GLM53_TF_MTP_PREFILL_CACHE=1) the rows only write the head's caches (``cache_absorb``)."""
+
+    if MTP_CACHE and cache_ok(e):
+        absorb_fn = cache_absorb
+    k = len(next_tokens)
+    skip = min(max(lo - p0, 0), k)
+    if skip == 0:
+        return absorb_fn(e, hidden, next_tokens)
+    st = e.st
+    if st.mtp_drafted:                           # as decode.absorb: drafted rows are not kept
+        st.set_mtp_len(st.mtp_len - st.mtp_drafted)
+        st.mtp_drafted = 0
+    from . import draftvocab
+
+    draftvocab.track(e.w, st, next_tokens[:skip])   # patches/0420: the skipped rows' tokens count for the rule too
+    s = st.mtp_len
+    if s + skip > st.mtp_kc.shape[0]:
+        raise ValueError("MTP window: the head's cache is full")
+    zero_mtp_rows(st, s, s + skip)
+    st.set_mtp_len(s + skip)
+    if skip == k:
+        return None
+    return absorb_fn(e, hidden[skip:], list(next_tokens[skip:]))
+
+
+# -- MTP prefill cache rows (GLM53_TF_MTP_PREFILL_CACHE, load-time) ----------------------------------------------
+#
+# A prefill absorbs every prompt position into the MTP head only for the head's caches: a row's cache entries (its
+# latent row, its indexer key and gate, the pools it completes) are functions of the row's own input (the main
+# model's hidden row and the next token) through row-local kernels, and prefill never reads the head's logits or
+# output rows (the pending last row is absorbed with its kept token in decode, by ``decode.draft``). So the head's
+# queries, index selection, sparse attention, o_proj, MoE (and their all-gathers) and final norm / lm_head over the
+# prompt were thrown away: ~90 ms a 2,048-row piece at 16k (5% of it), measured 2026-09-28 (results/W1). With this
+# switch prefill runs exactly the calls that produce the cache entries (the same functions on the same rows: the
+# same bits), and nothing after them. Decode, verify and drafting keep ``mtp.mtp_compute``. Both ranks must agree
+# (they would otherwise run different collectives): checked at load with ``load_settings``. Latent KV only (the
+# expanded cache keeps the full head); ``mtp_window`` still applies (rows below its start are zeroed, not written).
+
+CACHE_ENV = "GLM53_TF_MTP_PREFILL_CACHE"
+
+
+def mtp_cache_default() -> bool:
+    return bool(_int_env(CACHE_ENV, 0))
+
+
+MTP_CACHE = mtp_cache_default()
+
+
+def cache_ok(e) -> bool:
+    """Prefill's MTP rows can go through ``cache_absorb`` on this engine (latent KV, an MTP head, latent buffers)."""
+
+    w = getattr(e, "w", None)
+    if w is None or getattr(w, "mtp", None) is None or getattr(e, "mbuf", None) is None:
+        return False
+    meta = getattr(w, "meta", None)
+    return bool(meta.get("latent_kv")) if isinstance(meta, dict) else False
+
+
+def cache_absorb(e, hidden, next_tokens: Sequence[int]):
+    """``decode.absorb`` for prefill: the rows' head cache entries only, in chunks of the head's buffers, ``mtp_len``
+    advanced as ``absorb`` does. Returns None (prefill does not read the head's logits)."""
+
+    st = e.st
+    if st.mtp_drafted:                           # as decode.absorb: drafted rows are not kept
+        st.set_mtp_len(st.mtp_len - st.mtp_drafted)
+        st.mtp_drafted = 0
+    from . import draftvocab
+
+    draftvocab.track(e.w, st, next_tokens)          # patches/0420: the fallback rule's window (as decode.absorb)
+    step = e.mbuf.rows
+    for s0 in range(0, len(next_tokens), step):
+        part = list(next_tokens[s0:s0 + step])
+        mtp_cache_rows(e.w, st, e.mbuf, part, hidden[s0:s0 + step])
+        st.set_mtp_len(st.mtp_len + len(part))
+    return None
+
+
+def mtp_cache_rows(w, st, b, next_tokens: Sequence[int], hidden) -> None:
+    """``mtp.mtp_compute``'s calls up to the head's cache writes (latent row, indexer key / gate, pools), on the
+    same buffers and rows, and nothing after them: the cache entries have the full head's bits."""
+
+    from . import glue, latent, profile, qmm, sparse
+    from .forward import _join
+    from .mtp import mtp_stage
+
+    n = mtp_stage(w, st, b, next_tokens, hidden)
+    c = w.cfg
+    m = w.mtp
+    D = c.hidden
+    glue.embed(b.ids[:n], w.embed, D, 1, b.me[:n])
+    if b.zero_first:
+        b.me[0].zero_()
+    glue.rmsnorm(b.me[:n], m.enorm, c.eps, b.mcat[:n, :D])
+    glue.rmsnorm(b.hin[:n], m.hnorm, c.eps, b.mcat[:n, D:])
+    qmm.matmul(b.mcat[:n], m.eh, qmm.group_sums(b.mcat[:n], b.mxs[:n]), out=b.mx[:n], part=b.sk)
+    layer = m.layer
+    glue.rmsnorm(b.mx[:n], layer.in_norm, c.eps, b.normed[:n], b.xs[:n])
+    if profile.ON:
+        profile.lap("misc")
+    a = layer.dsa
+    # latent._project's first matmul and the kv norm (the q half is not needed), then _attend's cache write
+    qmm.matmul(b.normed[:n], a.proj, b.xs[:n], out=b.dp[:n], part=b.sk)
+    glue.rmsnorm(b.dp[:n, c.q_lora:], a.kv_norm, c.eps, b.lat[:n], b.xs_lat[:n])
+    latent.latent_write(b.lat[:n], st.mtp_kc, st.mtp_pos_dev)
+    if profile.ON:
+        profile.lap("dsa.proj")
+    if st.index is not None:                     # latent._index_proj, then _attend's index_update
+        ix = a.index
+        ik, ig, pk = st.index[-1]
+        qmm.matmul(b.normed[:n], ix.kw, b.xs[:n], out=b.ikr[:n], part=b.sk)
+        glue.router(b.normed[:n], ix.gate, b.igr[:n])
+        sparse.index_update(b.ikr[:n, :c.index_dim], b.igr[:n], ix.ln_w, ix.ln_b, ix.ape, ik, ig, pk, st.mtp_pos_dev)
+        if profile.ON:
+            profile.lap("dsa.indexer")
+    _join(w)
+
+
+def latent_tc_default() -> bool:
+    return bool(_int_env(TC_ENV, 0))
+
+
+def latent_tc(w) -> bool:
+    """A fast prefill on this engine runs the tensor-core latent absorb / expand (``latent.BF16_TC`` on a latent-KV
+    engine): its snapshot tag gets ``pfgrid.TC``. False without torch / the latent module (host fakes)."""
+
+    import sys
+
+    latent = sys.modules.get(__package__ + ".latent") if __package__ else None
+    if latent is None or not getattr(latent, "BF16_TC", False):        # never imported / off: host fakes, defaults
+        return False
+    meta = getattr(w, "meta", None)
+    return bool(meta.get("latent_kv")) if isinstance(meta, dict) else False
+
+
+def load_settings() -> list[int]:
+    """The load-time switches both ranks must agree on (they decide a fast prefill's bits)."""
+
+    return [int(latent_tc_default()), int(mtp_cache_default())]
+
+
+def settings() -> list[int]:
+    """The load-time defaults (both ranks print them; the per-request values travel in the header)."""
+
+    return [moe_glue_default(), mtp_window_default(), hc_default(), int(bm32_default())]
diff --git a/src/tensorfold/families/glm5_next/spark/pfgrid.py b/src/tensorfold/families/glm5_next/spark/pfgrid.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..adc8c37
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/tensorfold/families/glm5_next/spark/pfgrid.py
@@ -0,0 +1,264 @@
+"""Chunk plans, snapshot positions and snapshot tags of GLM-5.3-Flash prefills (patches/0085).
+
+Why a fast prefill's state does not depend on its chunk size
+------------------------------------------------------------
+patches/0080 kept resumed == fresh for fast (not row-invariant) prefills by putting chunks and snapshots on an
+absolute grid of the chunk size C: a request resumed only from a snapshot of its own C, and re-prefilled up to C - 1
+tokens of the old prompt on every turn. patches/0085 removes the need for that: every kernel a fast chunk runs is
+ROW-INDEPENDENT (a row's bits never depend on which other rows share the call, nor on how many there are) and the
+one kernel that couples rows, the chunked KDA scan, couples them only inside 64-row blocks at ABSOLUTE multiples of
+``ALIGN`` = 64:
+
+- ``fast_qmm.matmul_fast`` / ``matmul_fp8`` / ``hc_partial``, the latent ``absorb_tc`` / ``expand_tc``: tiles fixed
+  by the weight's shape, one accumulator walking K in a fixed order, per-row FP8 scales, no split-K, no atomics; and
+  (patches/0085) every call of a fast chunk runs them whatever its row count (``fastpf.chunk``: the < 64-row qmm
+  fallback, which gave a chunk's short tail other bits than the same rows inside a longer chunk, is gone; the head,
+  one row in every schedule, keeps qmm);
+- ``exl3_fast.cu``: a routed pair's gate/up/down is one warp's ascending mma chain over all of K; the expert's other
+  members only decide which warp and pass hold the pair; the Hadamard / SwiGLU epilogue is per element;
+- attention, the indexer's selection (patches/0065 row blocks select exactly), glue, hyper-connections, the router,
+  the bf16 gathers: the row-invariant kernels, or per-row arithmetic;
+- ``fast_kda``: 64-row blocks at absolute multiples of 64 (``off = pos % 64``); a block's bits depend only on its
+  rows and the fp32 state entering it, and a state handed between two calls is the fp32 value the one-call scan
+  keeps in registers. Every fast call starts at a multiple of 64 (chunk starts, cuts, marks, resume points, lean
+  sub-blocks), so the only partial block is the prompt's last one, the same in every schedule.
+
+Hence the committed state after a fast prefill of tokens t[0:n] (KDA states and conv windows, attention / indexer /
+MTP / DFlash2 caches, the first token) is a function of t[0:n] alone: the chunk size C is a speed choice, a chunk may
+be cut at any multiple of 64, and the state at any multiple of 64 is what every fast prefill of a prompt extending
+it holds there (the rows below it never read a later row).
+
+The rules (``plan``, ``decode._prefill``, ``engine._run``)
+---------------------------------------------------------
+1. Chunks: from the resume point (a multiple of 64), chunks of up to C rows (``chunk_rows``: the request's
+   ``prefill_rows`` rounded down to a multiple of 64, or ``auto``), also cut at the session store's marks and at
+   the snapshot point.
+2. Snapshots (fast): one per prefill, at S = the prompt's last multiple of ``snapshot_grid()`` G (default 64,
+   ``GLM53_TF_SNAPSHOT_GRID``): after the prefill when S = n, else before the chunk that starts at S, the prefill
+   cutting a chunk there when needed. Exception (``snapshot_tail()``, ``GLM53_TF_SNAPSHOT_TAIL``, default 256):
+   when the schedule's last chunk already starts within that many rows before S, the snapshot is taken there
+   instead (no extra chunk of fewer than G rows now; a next turn re-prefills at most tail + G - 1 more rows).
+   Positions past the prompt's last grid point are never kept, and neither is the reply (its rows were written by
+   the row-invariant decode kernels, not the fast chunks, so they are not what a fast prefill of the next prompt
+   holds): a next turn re-prefills the old prompt's last < G tokens (or < tail + G), the reply and its new tokens.
+3. Tags: exact snapshots 0, fast ones G, FP8 fast ones G + 1 (``tag``) -- by mode, never by C. A fast request
+   resumes from any snapshot with its tag at a multiple of 64 (``resumable``), whatever C made it.
+
+Claim: a fast prefill of p resumed from a snapshot at B (tag match, B a multiple of 64, p[:B] = its ids) ends in the
+fresh fast prefill's state. The snapshot holds the state of some fast prefill of a prompt q with q[:B] = p[:B] at B
+(by induction over the prefills that made it: each resumed one ended, at every position, in its fresh state); that is
+the fresh prefill of p's state at B (the rows below B depend on p[:B] only); from B on, the chunks may differ from the
+fresh prefill's, which does not change a bit. With patches/0080's argument for the caches (a request writes them only
+from its resume point on) this gives resumed == fresh; drafted == serial holds because the prefill is deterministic.
+
+With GLM53_TF_SNAPSHOT_GRID = C and a fixed C the snapshots, tags and chunks are exactly patches/0080's grid rule.
+
+patches/0540: the snapshot strictly before the prompt's end (GLM53_TF_SNAPSHOT_BEFORE_END, default 1)
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+A resume needs a snapshot of a STRICT prefix (``decode._prefill``: the first token is sampled from the prompt's last
+row, which a snapshot does not hold). Rule 2 put a prompt that ends on the grid (n = kG) at S = n, so an identical
+prompt sent again (a regenerate / retry, an agent resending its context, RigMark's "immediate replay") could not
+resume from it and fell back to the next session mark down (every 16,384 tokens): W13 replays resumed 0 / 16,384 /
+49,152 of 8,192 / 32,768 / 65,536 tokens. With ``before`` (the caller asks for it on the prefill that ends at the
+prompt's end: ``engine._run``, the batcher's last piece), S is the last grid point STRICTLY before n,
+(n - 1) // G * G, for every n, with rule 2's tail exception unchanged; so an on-grid prompt is treated exactly as
+the other G - 1 of every G lengths already were (one cut, snapshot at n - G), and a resend re-prefills at most G rows
+(or tail + G). The snapshot REPLACES the one at n (one per prompt, as before: no extra memory); a next turn that
+extends the prompt resumes G rows earlier than before, on 1 prompt length in G. Exact prefills (grid 0: a snapshot may
+sit anywhere) take theirs at the same S (a cut; exact chunks never depend on their cuts) instead of after the prompt.
+A cut and a snapshot at a multiple of 64 are what every other prompt length already gets: no new arithmetic, resumed
+== fresh as for every snapshot. Cost: one more chunk (one more read of the weights) on a prompt that ends on the grid
+and whose last chunk starts more than ``tail`` rows before S. Both ranks must agree (checked at load, ``engine``).
+
+Nothing here imports torch (the session store and host tests use it).
+"""
+
+from __future__ import annotations
+
+import os
+from dataclasses import dataclass, field
+from typing import Sequence
+
+ALIGN = 64                      # fast_kda's block: fast calls, cuts and fast snapshots sit on multiples of it
+AUTO = 0                        # prefill_rows "auto": the chunk size chosen per request (``chunk_rows``)
+FP8 = 1                         # added to the grid in an FP8 fast prefill's tag (fp8pf.TAG)
+TC = 2                          # patches/0190: added for a bf16 fast prefill with GLM53_TF_LATENT_TC (other bits)
+B12X = 4                        # patches/0240: + B12X x the b12x kernels' bits (1-7): offsets up to 2 + 28 < ALIGN
+GRID_ENV = "GLM53_TF_SNAPSHOT_GRID"
+TAIL_ENV = "GLM53_TF_SNAPSHOT_TAIL"
+DEFAULT_GRID = 64
+DEFAULT_TAIL = 256
+
+
+def snapshot_grid() -> int:
+    """GLM53_TF_SNAPSHOT_GRID (default 64, a multiple of 64): a fast prefill's snapshot sits at the prompt's last
+    multiple of it. Both ranks must agree (``settings``)."""
+
+    raw = os.environ.get(GRID_ENV, "").strip()
+    v = int(raw) if raw else DEFAULT_GRID
+    if v < ALIGN or v % ALIGN:
+        raise ValueError(f"{GRID_ENV}={raw}: expected a multiple of {ALIGN}")
+    return v
+
+
+def snapshot_tail() -> int:
+    """GLM53_TF_SNAPSHOT_TAIL (default 256, rows, >= 0): skip the cut at the snapshot point when the last chunk
+    already starts within this many rows before it (0: always cut)."""
+
+    raw = os.environ.get(TAIL_ENV, "").strip()
+    v = int(raw) if raw else DEFAULT_TAIL
+    if v < 0:
+        raise ValueError(f"{TAIL_ENV}={raw}: expected 0 or more rows")
+    return v
+
+
+BEFORE_ENV = "GLM53_TF_SNAPSHOT_BEFORE_END"
+
+
+def before_end() -> bool:
+    """patches/0540, GLM53_TF_SNAPSHOT_BEFORE_END (default 1): a whole prompt's snapshot sits at its last grid point
+    strictly before its end (0: at the end when it ends on the grid, as patches/0085)."""
+
+    raw = os.environ.get(BEFORE_ENV, "").strip()
+    if raw not in ("", "0", "1"):
+        raise ValueError(f"{BEFORE_ENV}={raw}: expected 0 or 1")
+    return raw != "0"
+
+
+def settings() -> list[int]:
+    """What both ranks must agree on (they decide the chunks, hence the collectives)."""
+
+    return [snapshot_grid(), snapshot_tail()]
+
+
+# -- tags -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+def tag(fast: bool, fp8: bool = False, grid: int | None = None, tc: bool = False, b12x: int = 0) -> int:
+    """A prefill's snapshot tag: 0 (exact), G (fast), G + 1 (FP8 fast), G + 2 (patches/0190: bf16 fast with the
+    tensor-core latent absorb / expand; FP8 fast chunks use those anyway); patches/0240: + 4 x the b12x kernels' bits
+    (1-7, ``b12xpf``), each a different arithmetic. Always below G + 64. Not the chunk size."""
+
+    if not fast:
+        return 0
+    g = snapshot_grid() if grid is None else int(grid)
+    if not 0 <= int(b12x) <= 7:
+        raise ValueError(f"snapshot tag: b12x bits {b12x}")
+    return (g + FP8 if fp8 else g + TC if tc else g) + B12X * int(b12x)
+
+
+def grid_of(t: int) -> int:
+    """The snapshot grid G of a tag (0 for exact snapshots): fast rows below a snapshot depend on the tokens up to the
+    end of their G-block at most (their 64-block, in fact)."""
+
+    return t - t % ALIGN
+
+
+def is_fp8(t: int) -> bool:
+    return bool(t) and t % ALIGN % B12X == FP8          # patches/0240: the b12x bits sit above the FP8 / TC offset
+
+
+def resumable(snap_tag: int, req_tag: int, pos: int) -> bool:
+    """A snapshot of ``snap_tag`` at ``pos`` may resume a prefill of ``req_tag``: same mode, and a fast one sits on a
+    multiple of 64 (any chunk size resumes from it)."""
+
+    return snap_tag == req_tag and (not req_tag or pos % ALIGN == 0)
+
+
+# -- the chunk size -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+def parse_rows(v) -> int:
+    """GLM53_TF_PREFILL_ROWS / ``tf_knobs.prefill_rows``: a row count (>= 1), or "auto" (``AUTO``)."""
+
+    if isinstance(v, str):
+        s = v.strip().lower()
+        if s == "auto":
+            return AUTO
+        v = int(s)
+    if isinstance(v, bool) or not isinstance(v, int) or v < 1:
+        raise ValueError(f"prefill rows {v!r}: expected a positive integer or \"auto\"")
+    return v
+
+
+def show_rows(rows: int):
+    """The knob's value as a request writes it: an int, or "auto"."""
+
+    return "auto" if rows == AUTO else int(rows)
+
+
+def chunk_rows(rows: int, todo: int, cap: int, fast: bool) -> int:
+    """The chunk size C of a prefill of ``todo`` tokens: ``rows`` (a count, or ``AUTO``) on buffers of ``cap`` rows.
+    Fast: a multiple of 64 (rows rounded down, at least 64); auto = the rows to prefill rounded up to 64, at most cap
+    rounded down to 64 (bigger chunks are never slower: each reads the weights once; the snapshot rule, not C, bounds
+    what a next turn re-prefills). Exact: rows capped at the buffers (auto: all of them); any C gives the same bits."""
+
+    if not fast:
+        return max(1, min(cap, todo if rows == AUTO else rows))
+    most = cap // ALIGN * ALIGN
+    if most < ALIGN:
+        raise ValueError(f"fast prefill: chunks are multiples of {ALIGN} rows, the buffers hold {cap}")
+    if rows == AUTO:
+        return max(ALIGN, min(most, -(-todo // ALIGN) * ALIGN))
+    c = max(ALIGN, rows // ALIGN * ALIGN)
+    if c > most:
+        raise ValueError(f"fast prefill: {c}-row chunks, the buffers hold {cap} rows")
+    return c
+
+
+# -- the plan -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+@dataclass
+class Plan:
+    """A prefill of positions [begin, n): its chunks, where its snapshot is taken (``snap``: begin = the resume
+    snapshot, or none when begin = 0; begin < snap < n: before the chunk starting there; n: after the prefill;
+    -1: none, exact prefills) and the marks it snapshots too (each the start of a chunk)."""
+
+    spans: list[tuple[int, int]]
+    snap: int
+    marks: list[int] = field(default_factory=list)
+    cut: bool = False                    # a chunk was cut at the snapshot point
+
+
+def spans(begin: int, n: int, step: int, cuts: Sequence[int] = ()) -> list[tuple[int, int]]:
+    """Chunks [start, stop) of up to ``step`` rows from ``begin``, also cut at every position in ``cuts``."""
+
+    out: list[tuple[int, int]] = []
+    start = begin
+    for q in sorted({c for c in cuts if begin < c < n}) + [n]:
+        while start < q:
+            stop = min(start + step, q)
+            out.append((start, stop))
+            start = stop
+    return out
+
+
+def plan(begin: int, n: int, step: int, *, fast: bool, marks: Sequence[int] = (), grid: int | None = None,
+         tail: int | None = None, before: bool = False) -> Plan:
+    """The chunks and snapshot of a prefill of positions [begin, n) in chunks of ``step`` rows (``chunk_rows``),
+    also snapshotting at ``marks`` (the session store's: exact anywhere, fast on multiples of 64). ``before``
+    (patches/0540): the prefill ends at the prompt's end and its snapshot must be of a strict prefix: S = the last
+    grid point strictly before n (exact prefills too, on the 64-grid; -1 when that is position 0 of a fresh one)."""
+
+    if not 0 <= begin < n or step < 1:
+        raise ValueError(f"prefill plan: positions {begin}..{n}, {step}-row chunks")
+    t = snapshot_tail() if tail is None else int(tail)
+    if not fast:
+        m = sorted({q for q in marks if begin < q < n})
+        if not before:
+            return Plan(spans(begin, n, step, m), -1, m)
+        # patches/0540: exact snapshots may sit anywhere; on the 64-grid as fast ones, always cut there (exact chunks
+        # are small by default, and the cut changes no bit); at or below the resume point the resume snapshot stays
+        s = (n - 1) // ALIGN * ALIGN
+        if s <= begin:
+            return Plan(spans(begin, n, step, m), begin if begin else -1, m)
+        base = spans(begin, n, step, m)
+        return Plan(spans(begin, n, step, m + [s]), s, [q for q in m if q != s],
+                    cut=all(a != s for a, _ in base))
+    if begin % ALIGN or step % ALIGN:
+        raise ValueError(f"fast prefill plan: resume point {begin} and chunk size {step} must be multiples of {ALIGN}")
+    g = snapshot_grid() if grid is None else int(grid)
+    m = sorted({q for q in marks if begin < q < n and q % ALIGN == 0})
+    base = spans(begin, n, step, m)
+    if n % g == 0 and not before:
+        return Plan(base, n, m)
+    s = (n - 1) // g * g                            # = n // g * g off the grid; n - g on it (patches/0540)
+    last = base[-1][0]
+    if last >= s or s - last <= t:
+        return Plan(base, last, [q for q in m if q != last])
+    return Plan(spans(begin, n, step, m + [s]), s, [q for q in m if q != s], cut=True)
