+"""G13 ``branches``: the attention sublayer's indexer / compressor chains on a side stream (``branches.py``,
+TF_DSV41_BRANCHES) on the GPU. Only the launch order and the overlap change, so everything here is bit for bit:
+
+- the fused q group (wq_b + the indexer's wq_b, one x3seg launch) == its two matrices as 1-segment launches, eager
+  and captured on two streams forked / joined in one graph, R 1..16; the counters return to zero;
+- e4's folded copies: ``_plain`` storing bf16 == float64 ``.to(fp32).to(bf16)``; ratio-2 pooling with the carry
+  through its own pointer on bf16 rows == the concatenated fp32 buffer (one slot and row mode);
+- the engine (the synthetic checkpoint, 4 slots on a KV pool): row graphs with branches on, replayed, == the eager
+  forward with branches off (logits, pending projection rows, kept carries), across context buckets and every row
+  bucket; the captured graph really forks (DOT dump: more fan-out nodes than the off graph);
+- batched == alone with branches on: a window of two slots gives each slot's rows the bits of that slot's window run
+  alone (row graphs on both).
+
+G14 (the unstable G13 1-row window; branches.py's G14 notes):
+- every mode (side stream at each TF_DSV41_BRANCHES_PRIO, and ``serial``: e4 alone) replayed == off eager, bit for bit;
+- the row graphs capture on the driver's main stream with the requested priorities, no fork is left open after
+  warm-up, replays and eager windows, and two engines built alike capture the same 1-row graph (nodes, edges,
+  fan-out / fan-in: the capture is deterministic);
+- [G14] lines: the streams' priorities, the device's priority range, whether the DOT dump carries node priorities.
