+"""M2 on the real forward (``decode.DecodeForward`` under ``batch.Batcher``) with DSpark, on the CPU twin of the
+kernels and a synthetic checkpoint holding ``mtp.*`` as the pack stores it (``dsv41_dspark_fakes``):
+
+- drafted == serial: DSpark rounds (3 blocks' pass, Markov + confidence heads, keyed draft noise, cost-derived
+  depth) give the serial reply token for token, at T = 0 and T > 0, past 2,048 tokens of context, with 1 slot and
+  with 4 slots decoding together; zero-depth rounds and skipped passes too;
+- lookup drafts == serial (deep windows of copied context), alone and mixed with DSpark rounds;
+- rollback: windows whose drafts are partly kept (an oracle drafter with a wrong token) == serial; after a partial
+  commit the drafter's context rings and the next drafts equal those of a forward that stepped serially;
+- two ranks (threads): both ranks draft the same tokens; the replies equal one rank's;
+- a snapshot carries the drafter's context (restore -> the same drafts);
+- the Engram prefetch: every read issued ahead is the one the forward asks for (no synchronous read), the same reply.
+"""
+
+from __future__ import annotations
+
+import numpy as np
+import pytest
+
+torch = pytest.importorskip("torch")
+pytestmark = pytest.mark.torch
